parent_id Schema
Every chunk ingested into ChromaDB gets:

parent_id = "{pagenumber}_{chunk_number}"
Example: page 3, 2nd chunk → "3_2"

Other metadata per chunk: 
page
 (int), chunk_idx, char_start, 
source
 (filename).

How the Functions Work
retrieve_chunks(query, top_k)
 — Fast Mode
Standard ChromaDB cosine similarity search. Returns the top_k closest chunks to the query.

deep_retrieve_chunks(query, top_k)
 — Deep Mode
Step 1  →  vector search (same as fast mode) → matched chunks
Step 2  →  for each matched chunk:
             page = parent_id.split("_")[0]   # e.g. "3"
             fetch ALL chunks WHERE metadata["page"] == page
Step 3  →  deduplicate + sort by (page, chunk_idx)
           → full section context in document order
This gives the LLM the full surrounding section, not just isolated snippets.

answer_question(question, mode="fast", top_k=3)
Routes to 
retrieve_chunks
 (fast) or 
deep_retrieve_chunks
 (deep)
Builds prompt capped at 8,000 chars
Calls Ollama LLM (model from OLLAMA_MODEL env var, default llama3)
Returns 
answer
, mode, top_k, 
sources
, 
chunks
Default is mode="fast" — existing behavior is unchanged.

